course: dictionary
lesson: 5672
title: Livestock: farm animals in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Livestock means animals kept on a farm for food, milk, wool or work, such as cows, sheep, pigs, goats and chickens. You can often work out a word like this from the words around it. «Old stories like Little Red Riding Hood come from times when people feared wolves and lost livestock.» Lost livestock means losing farm animals, so the wolves must have been taking them.
explain: «Livestock guardian dogs grow up with sheep and treat them as their family, barking at and chasing away foxes and other predators.» The sheep are livestock, and the dogs protect them. Ask yourself what word would fit: a farm animal, not a wild one. Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Livestock is an uncountable noun, so you do not say "two livestocks". You can use it with a singular or plural verb: «The livestock is safe in the barn» and «The livestock are safe in the barn» are both correct. A livestock farmer is a person who keeps these animals.
fact: Livestock means farm animals kept for food, milk, wool or work.
fact: Cows, sheep, pigs, goats and chickens are all examples of livestock.
fact: «The Laki eruption in Iceland in 1783-84 poured out poisonous gas that killed most of Iceland's livestock.» This is a true event from history.
fact: Farmers raise livestock, and livestock need food, water and shelter.
fact: Livestock is uncountable, so you can say "some livestock" but not "a livestock" when you mean the animals as a whole.
exercise: Which of these is livestock? | A goldfish in a bowl | A wild wolf in the forest | *A cow on a farm | A bird flying over the hills
exercise: «The Laki eruption killed most of Iceland's livestock.» What does livestock mean here? | Plants grown in fields | Wild birds that live in the hills | Farm tools and machines | *Farm animals such as sheep and cows
exercise: A farmer keeps 3 pigs and 2 goats as livestock. How many legs do they have altogether? | 10 | *20 | 12 | 15
test: Why do livestock guardian dogs bark at night? | *To chase away foxes and other predators | To help the sheep sleep | To find wild wolves in the forest | To wake the farmer for breakfast
test: What is a livestock farmer? | A person who sells wool in shops | A person who builds barns | *A person who keeps animals on a farm for food, milk, wool or work | A person who catches wild wolves
exam: Why did people in old stories fear wolves? | Because wolves carried their milk to the market | Because wolves ate their vegetables | Because wolves guarded their sheep | *Because wolves could kill their livestock
